                <pb facs="0634" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9311/583: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-19T16:00:00-04:00">June 19, 1935—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. For your information: On June 18 the Department, in reply to a note from
                    Minister Sze stating that the Chinese Government proposed to promote him to be
                    Ambassador to the United States, informed Minister Sze that this Government is
                    agreeable to such appointment.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d491-f1"/></p>
                <p>Inform Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
